# No Hardcoded Colors

All colors in this project MUST come from CSS custom properties defined in `app/globals.css` or the Tailwind semantic token system. Never write raw hex, rgb, hsl, or oklch color literals anywhere except in `app/globals.css`.

## Forbidden patterns (never write these):

```tsx
// ❌ Hex literals
style={{ color: '#D53F8C' }}
className="text-[#D53F8C]"

// ❌ RGB/RGBA
style={{ backgroundColor: 'rgb(213, 63, 140)' }}

// ❌ HSL
style={{ color: 'hsl(326, 68%, 54%)' }}

// ❌ Named colors except black/white
className="text-pink-500"   // ← use brand tokens instead
```

## Correct patterns (always use these):

```tsx
// ✅ Tailwind semantic tokens (mapped to CSS vars in globals.css)
className="text-primary"
className="bg-secondary"
className="border-brand-primary"

// ✅ CSS custom property reference in Tailwind arbitrary value
className="text-[var(--color-primary)]"

// ✅ Inline style with CSS var
style={{ color: 'var(--color-primary)' }}
```

## Brand token reference

| Token | CSS Variable | Value |
|-------|-------------|-------|
| Primary (Pink) | `--color-primary` / `var(--color-brand-primary)` | `#D53F8C` |
| Secondary (Blue) | `--color-secondary` / `var(--color-brand-secondary)` | `#00C5FA` |
| Background | `--color-background` | `#FFFFFF` |

## Where colors ARE allowed as literals

Only in `app/globals.css` inside `:root` / `.dark` / `@theme` blocks where the CSS custom properties are defined.
